    <h1>Brain Puzzle 3 Level 139 Answer: Office Holiday</h1>

    <div class="disclaimer">Unofficial fan-made guide. Not affiliated with the developer of Brain Puzzle 3.</div>

        <div class="answer-box">
      <span class="label">Quick answer</span>
      <p>Eleven moves. Tap the sunflower, drag the sun into the French window, lay the beach wallpaper on the floor, give the teddy bear's beach shirt to the male employee, tap the folder, put the barbecue poster on the floor, drop the boss's wig on the kitten, stand the butler cut-out next to the female employee, pour the water cup into the flower pot, hand a coconut to an employee, and finally throw the boss into the sea.</p>
    </div>
    <style is:global>
.answer-inline{margin:.55rem 0 0;padding:.6rem .9rem;background: #FFFBF2; border: 1px solid #F0DFAE; border-radius: 10px}
.answer-inline p{margin:0;font-size:14px;line-height:1.55;color:#7A6A5C}
.answer-inline a{color:#B45309;font-weight:800;text-decoration:underline}
    </style>
    <div class="answer-inline">
      <p>Got it? If you enjoy these, try <a href="/akari/">Akari</a>: our own free browser puzzle with a fresh grid every midnight. No app, no sign-up.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="verify-note">How this page was built: the clip below is 1:06 of unedited play, cut into one frame per second and read by hand. The eleven moves are the level's own hint list; the timestamps on the cards mark the beats we could confirm on screen, so the four cards without one are the moves that happen between our sampled frames.</div>

    <h2>Watch the full solution<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>An office on a stormy day, three staff, a boss, a cat and a teddy bear. The clip runs the whole level in under a minute — worth watching once before you start dragging.</p>
