    <h2>Level 139 walkthrough, move by move<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <!-- frame refs: hero=f_0010 (t=9s), sun=f_0016 (t=15s), grill/standee=f_0031 (t=30s), palm/coconut=f_0046 (t=45s), boss=f_0058 (t=57s), result=f_0066 (t=65s) -->
    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 1</span>
      <strong>Tap the sunflower</strong>
      <p>The level opens with a tap rather than a drag. The sunflower is the one prop in the office that looks like decoration and answers a single press, which is exactly why people spend a minute dragging the sun around instead. Tap it first and the room starts changing.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 2 &middot; 0:15</span>
      <strong>Drag the sun into the French window</strong>
      <img src="/brain-puzzle-3/l139_sun_window.jpg" alt="Brain Puzzle 3 level 139 step 2 — the window shows a beach" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="800" />
      <p>At nine seconds the window still shows a grey skyline with lightning over the city. By fifteen seconds it is a beach with sea and islands, because the sun went onto the glass. The window is the only surface in the room that accepts the sun; the desks and the employees ignore it.</p>
      <p class="ts">Video check: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2o7YsgRCKf8&t=15s" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">0:15</a></p>
    </div>
    <InContentAd />
    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 3</span>
      <strong>Lay the beach wallpaper on the floor</strong>
      <p>The wallpaper is the image on the computer screen at the back. Pull it off the monitor and drop it on the floor and the office carpet becomes sand. It is the one move in the level that changes the ground you are standing on rather than an object, so if the floor is still grey, this is the move you skipped.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 4 &middot; 0:57</span>
      <strong>Give the teddy bear's beach shirt to the male employee</strong>
      <img src="/brain-puzzle-3/l139_boss.jpg" alt="Brain Puzzle 3 level 139 step 4 — the staff are in beach clothes" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="800" />
      <p>The teddy bear on the designer's desk is already wearing the shirt you need. Drag it off the bear and onto the blond man at the keyboard; by the last quarter of the clip he is typing away in a Hawaiian shirt while the woman on the left ends the level in a sundress.</p>
      <p class="ts">Video check: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2o7YsgRCKf8&t=57s" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">0:57</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 5</span>
      <strong>Tap the folder</strong>
      <p>Second tap of the level: the folder on the desk opens and hands you something. Nothing in the room moves when you tap it except the folder itself, so it is easy to walk past — but the level does not finish without it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 6 &middot; 0:30</span>
      <strong>Drag the barbecue poster onto the floor</strong>
      <img src="/brain-puzzle-3/l139_grill_standee.jpg" alt="Brain Puzzle 3 level 139 step 6 — the barbecue grill on the office floor" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="800" />
      <p>The poster becomes a working grill once it is on the floor: by thirty seconds there is a lit barbecue with skewers smoking between the two desks, which is as close as this office gets to a summer party. The speech line under the scene switches to "Beach BBQ is a must" right after it lands.</p>
      <p class="ts">Video check: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2o7YsgRCKf8&t=30s" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">0:30</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 7 &middot; 0:30</span>
      <strong>Drop the boss's wig on the kitten</strong>
      <p>The boss has hair to spare and the cat sleeping by the desk has none. Drop the wig on the kitten and it lands as a grass hula skirt, which is the funniest single frame in the level. The cat is on the floor near the front desk, not on the desk itself.</p>
      <p class="ts">Video check: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2o7YsgRCKf8&t=30s" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">0:30</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 8 &middot; 0:30</span>
      <strong>Stand the butler cut-out next to the female employee</strong>
      <p>The life-size cut-out of the man in swim trunks and a towel starts near the window. Drag it next to the purple-haired designer and it stands there serving the scene; by thirty seconds it is already in place beside her desk.</p>
      <p class="ts">Video check: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2o7YsgRCKf8&t=30s" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">0:30</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 9 &middot; 0:45</span>
      <strong>Pour the water cup into the flower pot</strong>
      <img src="/brain-puzzle-3/l139_palm_coconut.jpg" alt="Brain Puzzle 3 level 139 step 9 — palm tree in the flower pot" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="800" />
      <p>The empty terracotta pot sits on the floor between the desks and the full glass sits on the desk above it. Drag the water down and a palm tree grows out of the pot. The pot never answers a tap; water is the only thing it wants.</p>
      <p class="ts">Video check: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2o7YsgRCKf8&t=45s" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">0:45</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 10 &middot; 0:45</span>
      <strong>Hand a coconut to an employee</strong>
      <p>The coconut comes off the palm once the tree is up. Drag it to any employee — the level accepts either of the two at the desks — and it appears as a coconut drink with a straw. By forty-five seconds there is one on each desk.</p>
      <p class="ts">Video check: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2o7YsgRCKf8&t=45s" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">0:45</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 11 &middot; 0:57</span>
      <strong>Throw the boss into the sea</strong>
      <img src="/brain-puzzle-3/l139_boss.jpg" alt="Brain Puzzle 3 level 139 step 11 — the boss out of his chair" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="800" />
      <p>The last move is the one nobody expects: the boss leaves his chair. Drag him through the window and he ends up swimming in the water behind the office, still in his suit, while the staff get on with the party. If your boss is still sitting at his screen, the level is one drag from done.</p>
      <p class="ts">Video check: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2o7YsgRCKf8&t=57s" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">0:57</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 12 &middot; 1:05</span>
      <strong>Level complete</strong>
      <img src="/brain-puzzle-3/l139_result.jpg" alt="Brain Puzzle 3 level 139 completed screen" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="800" />
      <p>The finished office freezes into the polaroid — grill smoking, palm in the pot, cat in a hula skirt, boss in the sea — and the banner reads Completed. Tap Next for level 140.</p>
      <p class="ts">Video check: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2o7YsgRCKf8&t=65s" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">1:05</a></p>
    </div>

    <h2>What makes Office Holiday tricky<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>Nothing here is hidden, and that is the problem. The office is full of ordinary things — a cup, a pot, a folder, a poster, a bear, a cat — and the level never says which ordinary thing is the interactive one. It asks for eleven moves and gives you a room where eight of the objects you can see do nothing at all, so the first minute is usually spent dragging the sun around a window that has not been told to accept it yet.</p>
    <p>The progressive part is the trap. The coconut does not exist until the palm does, and the palm does not exist until the pot has water in it. Players who try to hand out coconuts early find nothing to pick up and conclude the level is broken; the correct reading is that three moves are chained: water into the pot, tree out of the pot, coconut off the tree. The same goes for the barbecue, which is a flat poster until it is on the floor.</p>
    <p>And the last move inverts the whole scene: the boss is not a target for a decoration, he is the thing being removed. Every other character gets a summer accessory; he gets dropped into the sea. If you have done everything else and the level still will not end, look at the man in the chair at the front of the room — he is the one prop left that has not been touched.</p>

    <h2>Eleven moves in this order<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>This is the level's own hint list. The clip races through it in about forty seconds once the player knows the chain, so the timestamps on the cards are checkpoints rather than a schedule.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Tap the sunflower.</li>
      <li>Drag the sun into the French window.</li>
      <li>Put the beach wallpaper on the floor.</li>
      <li>Give the teddy bear's beach shirt to the male employee.</li>
      <li>Tap the folder.</li>
      <li>Drag the barbecue poster onto the floor.</li>
      <li>Drop the boss's wig on the kitten.</li>
      <li>Stand the butler cut-out next to the female employee.</li>
      <li>Pour the water cup into the flower pot.</li>
      <li>Hand a coconut to an employee.</li>
      <li>Throw the boss into the sea.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Three taps, eight drags, no hint items.</p>

